========================================================================
VERDICT
========================================================================

**FIXED** (path-A source close).

`c_parse_secret_env` still walks with `char_at` to classify ident chars after
line-start `// SECRET:`, then takes **one** `str_slice(src, start, k)` for
the ident span. There is no `name = name + c` / per-char OoStr concat in
the SECRET ident walk.

Directive match, space skip, fail-closed empty name, and
`__sec__` + `__secref__` env puts are unchanged.

Monofile `c_emit_secret.oo` = **264** lines (≤600; same as pre-fix;
already over soft 256 — did not grow).

